{\pard \fs18 \i File: public/faq.html\i0\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Meta title]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Motorcycle Wrap FAQ | K Films Jersey City\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Meta description]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 How much a motorcycle wrap costs, how long it takes, whether vinyl damages paint, helmet wraps, PPF and pickup \u8212? answered for riders in Jersey City and NYC.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Hero \u183? eyebrow]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Questions\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Hero \u183? h1]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 FAQ\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Hero \u183? lede]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 The things riders ask before booking. If yours isn\u8217?t here, ask it on the quote form \u8212? it costs nothing and there\u8217?s no obligation.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 How much does a motorcycle wrap cost?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 It depends on the bike and how much of it you want covered. A full colour change on a mid-complexity bike starts at $1,650, and partial wraps and accents start at $575. A faired sport bike takes more labour than a naked, because more bodywork has to come off. Send the bike and the idea through the quote form and you get a real number rather than a range.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 How long does wrapping take?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 A typical full colour change is 2\u8211?3 days in the garage once it starts. Partials and accents are quicker. You get a timeline in writing before any film is cut, and if a panel needs work before it can be wrapped you hear that first rather than on collection day.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Can you wrap individual fairings?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Yes. Single panels, a tank on its own, a tail section, or a two-tone split across the bodywork are all normal jobs. If you have a scratched panel and want it covered rather than the whole bike changed, that\u8217?s a partial wrap.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Can you wrap helmets?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Yes \u8212? helmet wraps are half of what this shop does. A helmet is compound curves in every direction, so it takes longer per square foot than a fairing, but the result is a lid nobody else has. We won\u8217?t wrap a helmet that has been dropped or is past its date.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Can my bike and helmet match?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 That\u8217?s the request we like most. Pick \u8220?Both\u8221? on the quote form and the design gets worked out across the two together, so the colours, the finish and the graphic placement line up rather than being applied twice separately.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Does vinyl damage paint?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Quality cast vinyl protects factory paint when it is installed and removed correctly. The risk is with paint that is already compromised \u8212? oxidised, previously resprayed badly, or lifting \u8212? because removal can take that with it. We will not wrap panels in that state without talking about it first.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 How long does vinyl last?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Cast films from the manufacturers we buy from are generally rated for several years on vertical surfaces, and how long yours actually lasts depends on sun, storage and washing. A bike kept outside all summer ages faster than one in a garage. We\u8217?ll tell you what to expect for the specific film you pick rather than quote a headline number.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 What is PPF?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Paint protection film \u8212? a clear, thicker film that goes over the areas that take physical damage rather than changing how the bike looks. On a motorcycle that usually means the tank where your knees and jacket buckle sit, and the leading edges that catch stones. It can go over paint or over a colour-change wrap.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Can you wrap over scratches?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Light scratches, yes. Vinyl is thin and it follows what is underneath, so deep scratches, dents and flaking clear coat will still read through the film \u8212? and a lifting edge will make the wrap fail early. Deeper damage needs sorting before the film goes on. Send photos with your quote and you\u8217?ll get a straight answer.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Do I need to remove my fairings?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 No \u8212? we do that here, and it is included in the labour. Taking panels off is what allows the film to wrap around the edge instead of being trimmed flush at it, which is the difference between a wrap that stays put and one that starts lifting.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Do you offer motorcycle pickup?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Yes. Ride or trailer it to the Jersey City garage at no charge, or we collect it \u8212? pickup starts at $75, and pickup with return delivery afterwards starts at $150. Either way it is quoted with the build, not charged up front. A bike that won\u8217?t start is still fine; say so and we bring the right kit.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 What areas do you serve?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 The garage is in Jersey City, and it is the only place the film gets cut. Brooklyn and New York City are pickup runs \u8212? there is no second shop in either. If you are outside that run, say where you are on the quote form and you\u8217?ll get an honest answer about whether we can reach you.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Do I need to know exactly what design I want?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 No, and most riders don\u8217?t. \u8220?Something dark with a red accent\u8221? is a fine starting point. Upload a photo of the bike and anything you like the look of \u8212? other bikes, colours, artwork \u8212? and we work it out from there. There is a \u8220?not sure\u8221? option on every question that needs one.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Do you wrap cars?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 No. Motorcycles and helmets only. The whole shop is set up around bodywork that comes off a bike.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Still deciding? \u183? Card \u183? Still deciding? \u183? h3]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Still deciding?\par}
