{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Brooklyn, NY, specifically \u183? Card \u183? The bike travels, the bench doesn't \u183? body]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Williamsburg, Bed-Stuy, Bushwick, Greenpoint, Park Slope, Crown Heights, Bay Ridge \u8212? pickup from Brooklyn starts at $75. Pickup with return delivery afterwards starts at $150, so the bike leaves your street and comes back to it without you crossing the river once.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Brooklyn, NY, specifically \u183? Card \u183? Nobody wants to ride to a wrap appointment \u183? h3]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Nobody wants to ride to a wrap appointment\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Brooklyn, NY, specifically \u183? Card \u183? Nobody wants to ride to a wrap appointment \u183? body]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 You could ride over the bridge and through the tunnel to drop it off, then work out how to get home, then do the whole thing again in reverse three days later. Or you could not. That\u8217?s the entire argument for pickup.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Brooklyn, NY, specifically \u183? Card \u183? Street-parked bikes get looked at properly \u183? h3]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Street-parked bikes get looked at properly\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Brooklyn, NY, specifically \u183? Card \u183? Street-parked bikes get looked at properly \u183? body]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 A bike that lives outside in Brooklyn has usually collected some things: scuffed tank edges, a mirror that met a van, oxidised plastics, a previous wrap someone rushed. Send photos with your build sheet and I\u8217?ll tell you what film will sit right and what needs sorting first \u8212? before you\u8217?ve paid anything.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? eyebrow]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Getting the bike here\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? h2]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Three ways, one of them free\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? lede]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Brooklyn is a pickup zone, not a location. The work happens in Jersey City and the quote will say so. Transport is quoted with the build, never charged up front.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? Card \u183? Ride it over yourself \u183? h3]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Ride it over yourself\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? Card \u183? Ride it over yourself \u183? body]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 If you don\u8217?t mind the trip to Jersey City, drop-off is free. Plenty of riders would rather not do it twice.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? Card \u183? I collect it \u183? h3]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 I collect it\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? Card \u183? I collect it \u183? body]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 The van comes to you and the bike goes back to the bench. Tell me where it\u8217?s parked and whether it runs.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? Card \u183? Collect and deliver back \u183? h3]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Collect and deliver back\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [Section \u183? Three ways, one of them free \u183? Card \u183? Collect and deliver back \u183? body]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Picked up before the build, delivered back after. You never move it yourself.\par}
