{\pard \fs22 Brooklyn, NY questions\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Do you have a Brooklyn shop?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 No. One garage, in Jersey City. Brooklyn is served by pickup \u8212? I collect the bike, wrap it there, and return it. Anyone telling you they have a bay in every borough is telling you something else.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 How much is pickup from Brooklyn?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 It starts at $75 one way, and $150 for collection plus return delivery. It\u8217?s quoted with the build rather than charged up front, and the exact number depends on where in Brooklyn you are and whether the bike is running.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 What if my bike isn't running?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Still fine, and it happens more than you\u8217?d think with a project bike. A bike that won\u8217?t start changes how I load it, not whether I come out. Put it in the pickup notes so I bring the right kit.\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? question]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 Can I come and watch the install?\par}
{\pard \fs18 \i [FAQ \u183? answer]\i0\par}
{\pard \fs22 You\u8217?re welcome at the garage while the bike is there, by arrangement. Most Brooklyn riders would rather see the film of it than sit in Jersey City for three days, which is why every build gets shot.\par}
